  <main>
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="hero" id="home" data-ux-law="Aesthetic-Usability Effect" data-ux-desc="The oversized typography, layered portraits, and bold negative space create an immediate emotional impression that makes the site feel crafted and personal.">
      <div class="hero__marquee-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="hero__marquee-row">
          <div class="hero__marquee-track">
            <span class="hero__marquee-text">Web Developer</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text">Web Developer</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text">Web Developer</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text">Web Developer</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__marquee-row">
          <div class="hero__marquee-track">
            <span class="hero__marquee-text hero__marquee-text--outline">UI/UX Designer</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text hero__marquee-text--outline">UI/UX Designer</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text hero__marquee-text--outline">UI/UX Designer</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text hero__marquee-text--outline">UI/UX Designer</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__marquee-row">
          <div class="hero__marquee-track">
            <span class="hero__marquee-text">AI Specialist</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text">AI Specialist</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text">AI Specialist</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text">AI Specialist</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__marquee-row">
          <div class="hero__marquee-track">
            <span class="hero__marquee-text hero__marquee-text--outline">Creative</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text hero__marquee-text--outline">Creative</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text hero__marquee-text--outline">Creative</span>
            <span class="hero__marquee-text hero__marquee-text--outline">Creative</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__images" data-ux-law="Serial Position Effect" data-ux-desc="The portraits sit at the top of the marquee rows, anchoring the most memorable part of the hero exactly where attention peaks.">
          <div class="hero__image hero__image--left">
            <img src="/assets/images/hero-1.png" alt="Amiruan portrait 1" loading="eager">
          </div>
          <div class="hero__image hero__image--center">
            <img src="/assets/images/hero-2.png" alt="Amiruan portrait 2" loading="eager">
          </div>
          <div class="hero__image hero__image--right">
            <img src="/assets/images/hero-3.png" alt="Amiruan portrait 3" loading="eager">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__scroll-hint">
        <span>Scroll</span>
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M19 12l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__bottom-bar" data-ux-law="Postel's Law" data-ux-desc="The bottom bar accepts loose scanning: visitors can read location, time, or status in any order they choose.">
        <div class="hero__bottom-left">
          <span>Based in Kuala Lumpur</span>
          <span>MYT (UTC+8)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__bottom-right">
          <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>Open to work</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Personal Quote -->
    <section class="quote-section" id="philosophy">
      <div class="container quote-section__inner reveal">
        <p class="quote-section__text" data-ux-law="Peak-End Rule" data-ux-desc="A memorable, personal statement early in the journey creates a strong emotional peak that shapes how visitors remember the experience.">
          "I'm not just a developer pushing pixels. I'm a <em>maker</em> who cares about how things feel, why they work, and what they mean for the people using them. Every interface is a conversation — I try to make it a good one."
        </p>
        <div class="quote-section__footer">
          <div class="quote-section__avatar">
            <img src="/assets/images/profile.png" alt="Amiruan profile">
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="quote-section__name">Muhammad Amiruddin</div>
            <div class="quote-section__role">Creative Web Developer & AI Specialist</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- About Section -->
    <section class="section" id="about">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-header reveal">
          <span class="section-label">01 — About</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">More than a <span class="coral-gradient-text">tech stack</span>.</h2>
          <p class="section-subtitle">I work across design, development, and AI — building every layer so nothing gets lost between handoff and launch.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="about-grid">
          <div class="about-text reveal" style="transition-delay: 100ms;">
            <p>
              I started out curious about why some websites felt effortless and others felt like work. That curiosity turned into a career: <strong>designing interfaces</strong> that respect attention, <strong>engineering WordPress systems</strong> that scale quietly, and <strong>weaving AI into workflows</strong> that actually help people.
            </p>
            <p>
              Based in Kuala Lumpur, I collaborate with founders, agencies, and product teams who want work that is fast, beautiful, and <em>human</em>. I don't chase trends. I chase clarity.
            </p>
            <p>
              When I'm not building, I'm learning — about typography, cognitive load, agentic systems, and the small details that make software feel like it was made for you.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="about-services reveal" style="transition-delay: 200ms;" data-ux-law="Hick's Law" data-ux-desc="Services are grouped into four clear, scannable items so visitors can quickly understand what I do without cognitive overload.">
            <div class="about-service">
              <span>Art Direction & UI/UX</span>
              <span class="about-service__arrow">→</span>
            </div>
            <div class="about-service">
              <span>Custom WordPress Engineering</span>
              <span class="about-service__arrow">→</span>
            </div>
            <div class="about-service">
              <span>AI Integration & Automation</span>
              <span class="about-service__arrow">→</span>
            </div>
            <div class="about-service">
              <span>Frontend Development</span>
              <span class="about-service__arrow">→</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Tri-Stack Matrix -->
    <section class="section" id="architecture">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-header reveal">
          <span class="section-label">02 — Core Disciplines</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">The <span class="coral-gradient-text">Tri-Stack</span> Matrix</h2>
          <p class="section-subtitle">Three disciplines I combine to ship complete digital products.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="matrix" data-ux-law="Law of Common Region" data-ux-desc="Each discipline is visually enclosed in its own card with shared borders and spacing, making the three pillars feel like a unified group.">
          <article class="matrix-card reveal" style="transition-delay: 100ms;">
            <div class="matrix-card__icon">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M12 19l7-7 3 3-7 7-3-3z"></path>
                <path d="M18 13l-1.5-7.5L2 2l3.5 14.5L13 18l5-5z"></path>
                <path d="M2 2l7.586 7.586"></path>
                <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="2"></circle>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="matrix-card__title">UI/UX Design</h3>
            <p class="matrix-card__desc">Human-centered interfaces with intentional motion, accessible patterns, and design systems that scale.</p>
            <ul class="matrix-card__list">
              <li>Figma Design Systems</li>
              <li>Micro-Interactions & Motion</li>
              <li>Responsive Layouts</li>
              <li>Accessibility (a11y)</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="matrix-card reveal" style="transition-delay: 200ms;">
            <div class="matrix-card__icon matrix-card__icon--sage">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16z"></path>
                <polyline points="3.27 6.96 12 12.01 20.73 6.96"></polyline>
                <line x1="12" y1="22.08" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="matrix-card__title">WordPress Engineering</h3>
            <p class="matrix-card__desc">Headless and monolithic architectures, custom content models, and backend automation that just works.</p>
            <ul class="matrix-card__list">
              <li>ACF Pro & Custom Post Types</li>
              <li>Headless REST / GraphQL</li>
              <li>Custom Hooks & Filters</li>
              <li>Dockerized Workflows</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="matrix-card reveal" style="transition-delay: 300ms;">
            <div class="matrix-card__icon matrix-card__icon--lavender">
              <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"></line>
                <line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"></line>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="matrix-card__title">AI Integration</h3>
            <p class="matrix-card__desc">Agentic assistants, real-time interfaces, and generative components that feel helpful, not robotic.</p>
            <ul class="matrix-card__list">
              <li>LLM Agent Prompting</li>
              <li>WebSocket Systems</li>
              <li>Vector Embeddings & RAG</li>
              <li>Interactive Kiosks</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Selected Works -->
